 The label token to a lot of our customers doesn't mean anything.

88
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,820
 They feel that they're buying chips to go to the casino.

89
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:26,820
 And they feel that somehow they're getting screwed but they don't quite understand how.

90
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:28,820
 And I think that actually reflects reality.

91
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,820
 Nobody really understands what a token is.

92
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:33,820
 You can only retrospectively analyze how it's calculated.

93
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:37,820
 There's so many problems with tokens as a pricing mechanism.

94
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:42,820
 And the biggest problem for CFOs who get the bill is it's like,

95
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:45,820
 what the fuck have I just spent all this money on?

96
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:47,820
 What's the value back to my organization?

97
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:50,820
 So we've done something very different in our business.

98
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:53,820
 Where we have customers using consumption pricing.

99
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:57,820
 We're charging them by the hour saved and the hour of human time equivalent.

100
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:04,820
 And that means that if you're paying for tokens and you're asking the AI to dig 10 holes and fill them in again.

101
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:08,820
 You're paying for all of that work which was completely unnecessary.

102
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:14,820
 Whereas if you're paying for the time that is being done.

103
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:18,820
 You really think about every task in terms of its human equivalence.

104
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:19,820
 And you're asking yourself the question.

105
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,820
 Would I have asked a human to have done this?

106
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:29,820
 And so when we bill our customers and give them a bill for 150 hours of human time saved.

107
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:31,820
 We charge less than minimum wage.

108
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:35,820
 So there's always an implicit ROI built into that.

109
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:40,820
 And I think the whole question about pricing for AI is going to evolve over the coming years.

110
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:47,820
 But my bet is that we're going to start to move to a model which is much more intuitive for us as humans to understand.

111
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:54,820
 Like our time equivalent as opposed to something which is a made up metric like tokens.

